# Boscali Summer, chapter 2: Heartland. Chapter 1 is summer-wing.scenario.
# A scripted opening on top of the game's own Escalation mission, which then opens into the full war.
# The format is documented in docs/SCENARIOS.md. Copy this file to BepInEx/config/BoscaliSummer/scenarios/
# and edit it there to change the mission: a file with the same scenario id replaces this one.

scenario boscali-summer
title "Boscali Summer"
base "Escalation"
group "Boscali Summer"
campaign boscali-summer 2

about
| June 2034. The Boscali Republic, fifty-two million people on one archipelago, went to bed under one flag and woke under two.
| PALA's coup took the outer islands in a night and most of Heartland in three weeks. Agrapol, the capital, fell on day nine.
|
| On day twenty-two the Home Fleet came in out of a storm with its transponders dark, and it had not changed sides. The Republic
| holds the north shore again and the front runs through the middle of the island. PALA is still the stronger army. It is also,
| for the first time, going backwards.
|
| You fly for Tradewind Air Services, and both sides are hiring. Pick one. The first sorties are handed to you; after that the war is yours.
|
| Victory: destroy every enemy aircraft factory, then sink the fleet carrier that arrives to save them. Score unlocks heavier
| airframes and, in the end, warheads.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ the world
# Everything in this part is written into the copy of Escalation before it loads; the game itself runs it.

time 7.4
weather 0.22
# Seconds between the war being decided and the end screen, so the last transmission is heard.
ending 16

# Escalation hands both sides their first target at once. Here that waits until the opening is flown.
hold Destroy_PALA_HWY1 Destroy_BDF_HWY2 Destroy_BDF_South
begin bdf_patrol pala_patrol bdf_sortie1 bdf_sortie2 pala_sortie1 pala_sortie2 curtain

# The counter-offensive starts today, so armour is already on the roads: a copy of two of Escalation's reinforcement columns a side
# rolls out of Maris and North Boscali, and out of Agrapol and Sandrift, as the mission starts. The columns Escalation sends later
# still come. The radar missile launchers stay home: the opening is flown in light aircraft.
copy SpawnConvoyFromCityToEastFront     as push_bdf_maris   without=RadarSAM1
copy SpawnConvoyFromNorthToEastFront    as push_bdf_north   without=RadarSAM1
copy SpawnConvoyFromMountainToEastFront as push_pala_agrapol without=RadarSAM1
copy SpawnConvoyFromDesertToEastFront   as push_pala_sandrift without=RadarSAM1

# The raids of the opening: three light attack aircraft a side, copies of the ones parked on the two highway strips. They appear low
# in the gap between the two armies, six kilometres from the picket station: close enough to meet the pilot before the air defence
# of the strip has dealt with all of them.
unit raid_pala_1 like COIN   at 16700 480  900 heading=10  speed=95 skill=0.7 fuel=0.6
unit raid_pala_2 like COIN   at 16950 520  600 heading=10  speed=95 skill=0.7 fuel=0.6
unit raid_pala_3 like COIN   at 16450 540  500 heading=10  speed=95 skill=0.7 fuel=0.6
unit raid_bdf_1  like COIN_2 at 15700 480 3900 heading=195 speed=95 skill=0.7 fuel=0.6
unit raid_bdf_2  like COIN_2 at 15450 520 4200 heading=195 speed=95 skill=0.7 fuel=0.6
unit raid_bdf_3  like COIN_2 at 15950 540 4250 heading=195 speed=95 skill=0.7 fuel=0.6

# --- the Republic's opening: fly to the picket station south of K92, break the raid that comes for the strip
objective bdf_patrol bdf "Fly to the picket station" reach 17600 600 7000 range=3000
  then spawn raid_pala_1 raid_pala_2 raid_pala_3
  then start bdf_raid bdf_raid_clock
objective bdf_raid bdf "Break the raid on K92" destroy raid_pala_1 raid_pala_2 raid_pala_3
  then stop bdf_raid_clock
  then start bdf_handoff
# Raiders that run for home must not hold the story up.
objective bdf_raid_clock wait 420
  then finish bdf_raid
objective bdf_handoff wait 30
  then start Destroy_PALA_HWY1

# --- PALA's opening, the mirror: the picket station north of Dustbowl, and the raid that comes for that strip
objective pala_patrol pala "Fly to the picket station" reach 14500 600 -2400 range=3000
  then spawn raid_bdf_1 raid_bdf_2 raid_bdf_3
  then start pala_raid pala_raid_clock
objective pala_raid pala "Break the raid on Dustbowl" destroy raid_bdf_1 raid_bdf_2 raid_bdf_3
  then stop pala_raid_clock
  then start pala_handoff
objective pala_raid_clock wait 420
  then finish pala_raid
objective pala_handoff wait 30
  then start Destroy_BDF_HWY2 Destroy_BDF_South

# A side nobody flies for, or a pilot who goes their own way, still gets the war: nine minutes in, the held targets start anyway.
objective curtain wait 540
  then start Destroy_PALA_HWY1 Destroy_BDF_HWY2 Destroy_BDF_South

# Landed sorties are how the story knows a pilot is settling in: the first one, then 120 points of them.
objective bdf_sortie1 bdf sortie 1
objective bdf_sortie2 bdf sortie 120
objective pala_sortie1 pala sortie 1
objective pala_sortie2 pala sortie 120

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ the story
# Everything below is each pilot's own screen: nothing here changes the world.

cast broker   command "BROKER"   "Tradewind Air Services"
cast anvil    command "ANVIL"    "BDF Northern Command"
cast citadel  command "CITADEL"  "PALA Heartland Command"
cast skywatch awacs   "SKYWATCH" "Air picture"

# The photographs of the opening: the mod's own event paintings, pinned up one by one as the days go by.
picture coup      poster press_censorship
picture capital   poster emergency_withdrawal
picture stretched poster frontline_overstretch
picture fleet     poster merchant_fleet_charter
picture hired     poster veteran_contractor_influx

shot port     orbit airbase "Maris Airport"     radius=2200 height=520 from=20  to=70  seconds=8
shot capital  orbit airbase "Agrapol Airbase"   radius=2400 height=650 from=200 to=250 seconds=9
shot occupier orbit unit push_pala_agrapol_2    radius=150  height=55  from=120 to=200 seconds=9 fov=34
shot front    fly 15400 650 -2200 to 16700 560 5200 look 17900 180 11500 seconds=9
shot fleet    orbit unit SmallCarrier1          radius=420  height=95  from=250 to=330 seconds=9
shot column   orbit unit push_bdf_maris_2       radius=150  height=55  from=300 to=380 seconds=9 fov=34
shot strip    orbit airbase "K92 Highway Strip" radius=1300 height=320 from=140 to=185 seconds=7

# The opening plays every time (Space skips it), then the pilot picks a side on the script's own plate. It is told the evening before, in the storm that
# brought the fleet in: the host's sky and clock are set for it, and put back for the morning the mission is flown in.
beat intro when start
  music "synthetic-warfront.mp3"
  clock 17.45
  sky storm
  cut port     "The Boscali Republic" "June 2034. Fifty-two million people. One archipelago. One summer left."
  cut capital  "02:10. Every relay tower in the outer islands goes dark in the same second. By sunrise PALA owns the networks, the ports, and the story." photo=coup stamp="OUTER ISLANDS - 02 JUN 2034 / DAY 1" fx=glitch
  cut occupier "The capital lasts nine days. The government leaves Agrapol by the north road, in whatever still has charge." photo=capital stamp="AGRAPOL - 10 JUN 2034 / DAY 9" fx=lost
  cut front    "PALA's armour outruns its own supply drones. The advance stops forty kilometres short of the last free port." photo=stretched stamp="THE NORTH SHORE - 21 JUN 2034 / DAY 20"
  cut fleet    "Then the Home Fleet comes in out of the storm, transponders dark. Nobody had thought to ask the navy whose side it was on." photo=fleet stamp="MARIS ROADS - 23 JUN 2034 / DAY 22" fx=alert
  cut column   "At first light the Republic goes south. Both armies have run out of pilots. Neither has run out of money." photo=hired stamp="MARIS - 24 JUN 2034 / DAY 23" fx=warm
  cut strip    "Boscali Summer" "Pick a side."
  dip
  clock 7.4
  sky clear
  card "Day twenty-three" "First light. The storm has blown out to sea." seconds=4
  choose

# --- flying for the Republic
beat bdf-brief when join side=bdf
  say broker "Ink is dry. Tradewind Air Services now flies for the Republic. Try to look like you believe in something."
  say anvil "Tradewind, this is Anvil, Northern Command. Three weeks ago we lost the capital. Yesterday the fleet came home. Today we start taking the island back."
  say anvil "Pick an airframe and get up. Your picket station is south of the K92 strip, and it is marked. K92 and Maris are the closest fields. Keep it low near the front: above the hills, the sky belongs to the missiles."
  hint "Choose an airbase and an aircraft. The picket station is marked on the map and in your objectives."

beat bdf-up when airborne side=bdf unless=open
  say broker "The company pays for the wing. Hold C for the ring: weapons, flight, wing, comms. The wingmen do what the ring says. Mostly."

beat bdf-contact when done bdf_patrol side=bdf
  say skywatch "Skywatch. Three bandits out of Dustbowl, low and fast, nose on K92. Light attack. Air defence is reaching for them. Get your share before the missiles do."
  say anvil "Break that raid before it reaches the strip. Weapons free."

beat bdf-raid-done when done bdf_raid side=bdf
  say skywatch "Picture is clean. The raid is finished."
  say anvil "Good. Now we return the visit. Dustbowl strip: the depots, and the gun that guards them. It is going on your board."
  say broker "That was the audition. From here it is an open contract: fly what you like, hit what pays. I will call when the invoice changes."
  flag open

beat bdf-dustbowl when done Destroy_PALA_HWY1 side=bdf
  say anvil "Dustbowl strip is down and the armour is rolling south. Next, the vehicle plants behind it. Every truck that burns there never reaches the front."

beat bdf-sandrift when done Destroy_PALA_AirbaseDesert side=bdf
  say anvil "Sandrift is out of the war. The whole east coast is open."

beat bdf-capital when done Destroy_PALA_AirbaseMtn side=bdf
  say anvil "Agrapol's defences are down. They held our capital for a month. They will not hold it for another day."
  say broker "Somebody at Northern Command just wept on an open channel. I am billing them for it."

beat bdf-fleet when done SendNavalReinf side=bdf
  say anvil "The carrier group is on station with the fleet's air wing. So is theirs. A fleet carrier is the last card PALA holds."

beat bdf-endgame when started SinkPALACarrier side=bdf
  say anvil "Their factories are gone. That carrier is all PALA has left on this side of the water. Sink her, and Heartland is ours."

beat bdf-won when done BDF_Victory_Conditions side=bdf
  remember flew-bdf
  finish
  say anvil "All stations, Anvil. PALA forces on Heartland have ceased fire. The island is the Republic's again."
  say broker "One island down and a great many to go. I will draw up the next contract. Go and sleep."

beat bdf-lost when done PALA_Victory_Conditions side=bdf
  say anvil "All stations. Northern Command is going off the air. It was an honour."
  say broker "The Republic's cheque just bounced. Get to the coast. I will find us a boat."

# --- flying for PALA
beat pala-brief when join side=pala
  say broker "Ink is dry. Tradewind Air Services now flies for PALA. They pay on time, which is more than I can say for their manners."
  say citadel "Tradewind, this is Citadel, Heartland Command. We took this island in three weeks. The Republic's navy thinks it can take it back in three days."
  say citadel "Get airborne. Your picket station is north of the Dustbowl strip, and it is marked. Dustbowl and The Farm are the closest fields. Stay low near the front: above the hills, the sky belongs to the missiles."
  hint "Choose an airbase and an aircraft. The picket station is marked on the map and in your objectives."

beat pala-up when airborne side=pala unless=open
  say broker "The company pays for the wing. Hold C for the ring: weapons, flight, wing, comms. The wingmen do what the ring says. Mostly."

beat pala-contact when done pala_patrol side=pala
  say skywatch "Skywatch. Three bandits off K92, low, running south at Dustbowl. Light attack. Air defence is reaching for them. Get your share before the missiles do."
  say citadel "That is their opening move. Stop it short of the strip."

beat pala-raid-done when done pala_raid side=pala
  say skywatch "Picture is clean. The raid is finished."
  say citadel "Acceptable. Now break their footholds before the fleet can feed them: the K92 strip, and the airfield at South Boscali. Both are on your board."
  say broker "That was the audition. From here it is an open contract: fly what you like, hit what pays. I will call when the invoice changes."
  flag open

beat pala-k92 when done Destroy_BDF_HWY2 side=pala
  say citadel "K92 is closed. Their road south is cut. The plants that feed it are next."

beat pala-south when done Destroy_BDF_South side=pala
  say citadel "South Boscali has fallen. Their flank is gone."

beat pala-maris when done Destroy_BDF_AirbaseCity side=pala
  say citadel "Maris Airport is finished. The fleet has nowhere left to land its wounded."
  say broker "The harbour master of Maris wants to know who pays for his windows. I gave him your name."

beat pala-fleet when done SendNavalReinf side=pala
  say citadel "Our fleet carrier is on station. So is the rest of their navy. Hold the island until one of the two is on the bottom."

beat pala-endgame when started SinkBDFCarrier side=pala
  say citadel "Their factories are ash. The carrier is the last thing the Republic owns in these waters. Sink it, and the counter-offensive ends."

beat pala-won when done PALA_Victory_Conditions side=pala
  remember flew-pala
  finish
  say citadel "All stations, Citadel. The Republic's forces on Heartland have laid down their arms. The island holds."
  say broker "Paid in full. For the record, I would have taken either side's money. So would you."

beat pala-lost when done BDF_Victory_Conditions side=pala
  say citadel "All stations. Heartland Command is closing down. Destroy your ciphers."
  say broker "Time to be somewhere else. I know a strip on an island nobody has couped yet."

# --- both sides: the war opens up one system at a time
beat naval-warning when started SendNavalReinf
  say skywatch "All stations, Skywatch. Big decks inbound from both ends of the strait. Ten minutes."

beat bdf-first-sortie when done bdf_sortie1 side=bdf
  flag first-sortie
beat pala-first-sortie when done pala_sortie1 side=pala
  flag first-sortie
beat ops-open when flag first-sortie
  say broker "You brought it back in one piece, so you get paid. Command has opened the support net to you: satellites, hackers, and people with rifles."
  hint "OPS on the map: support calls, fronts and readiness."

beat bdf-proven when done bdf_sortie2 side=bdf
  flag proven
beat pala-proven when done pala_sortie2 side=pala
  flag proven
beat str-open when flag proven
  say broker "The staff has noticed you. They want you looking at the whole board, not one runway."
  hint "STR on the map: theater command, territory and where the front is going."

beat desk when time 780 if=open
  say broker "Side work is posted on the task desk when you want it. Contracts are optional. So is eating."
